 Day 5 — AWS Lambda + Serverless Architecture

Scenario-Based DevOps Interview Questions

1️⃣ Your application needs to run backend logic without managing servers. How will you decide if Lambda is the right compute choice over EC2 or ECS?

2️⃣ A Lambda function is frequently timing out due to long-running operations. What optimizations or architectural changes will you apply?

3️⃣ You must process millions of S3 object upload events per day. How will you design a scalable concurrency and event-handling model?

4️⃣ API latency is inconsistent because Lambda cold starts are high. What strategies will you use to reduce or avoid cold starts?

5️⃣ A Lambda + API Gateway architecture is facing throttling during peak traffic. How will you troubleshoot and scale this solution?

6️⃣ A Lambda function needs to connect to RDS inside a VPC. How will you configure networking and prevent slow ENI cold starts?

7️⃣ You need to build a fan-out event architecture where one event triggers multiple workflows. How will you design this with SNS or EventBridge?

8️⃣ A Lambda function must run automatically every hour. Which AWS service will you use to schedule it?

9️⃣ Your Lambda function is hitting memory and time limits while processing large files. What architectural redesign will you propose?

🔟 Lambda must call external APIs securely without exposing credentials. How will you manage secrets?

1️⃣1️⃣ A Lambda deployment introduced a production outage. How will you implement safe deployment strategies like versioning and rollbacks?

1️⃣2️⃣ You need full distributed tracing for Lambda-based microservices. Which AWS services will you use to enable this?

1️⃣3️⃣ Lambda cost has increased due to high invocation volume. What techniques will you use to optimize cost?

1️⃣4️⃣ A Lambda function must write to DynamoDB at extremely high throughput. How will you avoid throttling?

1️⃣5️⃣ You need to design an event-driven workflow using S3 → Lambda → Step Functions. How will you implement retries and error handling?

